From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Print the message timestamp with a 64-bit format

The debug line for every processed message printed the time_t
timestamp with "%ld". Where long is 32 bits but time_t is 64 bits, as
on 32-bit Linux built with _TIME_BITS=64 (gcc warns there with
-Wformat), the arguments after it were read from the wrong place, so
the "%s" for the text could read a bogus pointer.

Cast the timestamp to gint64 and use G_GINT64_FORMAT.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/hoehermann/purple-gowhatsapp/pull/303]
---
 glue/process_message.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/glue/process_message.c b/glue/process_message.c
index 8fa809f..be20534 100644
--- a/glue/process_message.c
+++ b/glue/process_message.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ gowhatsapp_process_message(gowhatsapp_message_t *gwamsg)
         return;
     }
     purple_debug_info(
-        GOWHATSAPP_NAME, "recieved %s (subtype %d) for account %p remote %s (isGroup %d) sender %s (alias %s, isOutgoing %d) sent %ld: %s\n",
+        GOWHATSAPP_NAME, "recieved %s (subtype %d) for account %p remote %s (isGroup %d) sender %s (alias %s, isOutgoing %d) sent %" G_GINT64_FORMAT ": %s\n",
         gowhatsapp_message_type_string[gwamsg->msgtype],
         gwamsg->subtype,
         gwamsg->account,
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ gowhatsapp_process_message(gowhatsapp_message_t *gwamsg)
         gwamsg->senderJid,
         gwamsg->name,
         gwamsg->isOutgoing,
-        gwamsg->timestamp,
+        (gint64)gwamsg->timestamp,
         gwamsg->text
     );
 
